  "content": {
    "id": "p4-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Consider an arbitrary polynomial\n$$P(x)=a_nx^n+a_{n-1}x^{n-1}+\\cdots+a_1x+a_0.$$\nRecall that a function is even if $f(-x)=f(x)$ for all $x\\in\\mathbb R$, and odd if $f(-x)=-f(x)$ for all $x\\in\\mathbb R$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p4-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Give an example of an even polynomial with two terms.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "For example, $f(x)=x^4+x^2$.",
          "worked": "Choose two even powers of $x$, for example $f(x)=x^4+x^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=(-x)^4+(-x)^2\\\\f(-x)&=x^4+x^2\\\\f(-x)&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nThus $f$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Give an example of an odd polynomial with two terms.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "For example, $f(x)=x^3+x$.",
          "worked": "Choose two odd powers of $x$, for example $f(x)=x^3+x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=(-x)^3+(-x)\\\\f(-x)&=-x^3-x\\\\f(-x)&=-f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nThus $f$ is odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "State (but do not prove) a general condition for a polynomial to be even.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "All coefficients of odd powers of $x$ are zero.",
          "worked": "A polynomial is even if and only if every odd-power coefficient is zero. Its nonzero terms therefore contain only even powers of $x$, including a possible constant term.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q14-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "State (but do not prove) a general condition for a polynomial to be odd.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "All coefficients of even powers of $x$, including the constant term, are zero.",
          "worked": "A polynomial is odd if and only if every even-power coefficient is zero, including $a_0$. Its nonzero terms therefore contain only odd powers of $x$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      }
    ]
  },
